cial character. The space ( ) is one of the more important nonprinting characters.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="85464">nonprinting character</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463043">чыгарылбоочу символ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11241_85464_463044"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A character used to control the format of displayed or printed information, rather than to represent a particular letter, digit, or other special character. The space ( ) is one of the more important nonprinting characters.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="85464">nonprinting character</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463044">басып чыгарылбоочу символ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11245_59333_462841"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A sequence of shades ranging from black through white, used in computer graphics to add detail to images or to represent a color image on a monochrome output device.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="59333">grayscale</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="462841">б