l within a graphical user interface that when clicked remains "down" (appearing to be pressed) until it is clicked again.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2766794">toggle switch</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2770358">өйдө-ылдый которгуч</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11305_2766794_463481"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An on/off control within a graphical user interface that when clicked remains "down" (appearing to be pressed) until it is clicked again.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2766794">toggle switch</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463481">өчүрүп/күйгүзүү баскычы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11310_232414_463720"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to items that occur repeatedly. For example, an appointment or task that occurs on a regular basis, such as a weekly status meeting or a monthly haircut, can be designated as recurring.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232414">recurring</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463720">кайталанг