ет протоколу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1379_120227_463252"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The suite of networking protocols arranged in four layers, which are called the link layer, internet layer, transport layer, and application layer, and that includes IP in the internet layer and TCP in the transport layer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="120227">TCP/IP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463252">TCP/IP протоколу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1379_120228_1493669"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The suite of networking protocols arranged in four layers, which are called the link layer, internet layer, transport layer, and application layer, and that includes IP in the internet layer and TCP in the transport layer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="120228">Transmission Control Protocol/Internet Protocol</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1493669">TCP протоколу/Интернет протоколу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1379_120228_463252"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The suite of networking protocols arranged in four layers, which are called the link layer, internet layer, transport layer, and application layer, and that includes IP in the internet layer and TCP in the transport layer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="120228">Transmission Control Protocol/Internet Protocol</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463252">TCP/IP протоколу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13805_135723_463348"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To adjust the perspective of an image or document in order to view a larger area on the screen at one time, as if viewed from farther away.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="135723">zoom out</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463348">кичирейтүү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13809_88455_1494213"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The menu choice that allows a user to customize application behavior.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="88455">Options</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1494213">Параметрлер</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13821_137076_1944422"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The sheet that you're working on in a workbook. The name on the tab of the active sheet is bold.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="137076">active sheet</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1944422">иштелип жаткан барак</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13829_237385_1494214"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A customizable toolbar that provides one-click access to commands.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="237385">Quick Access Toolbar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1494214">Ыкчам мүмкүндүк алуу куралдар панели</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13835_141250_463416"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A control on a menu, toolbar, dialog box, or data access page that displays a list of options when you click the small arrow next to the list box.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="141250">drop-down list box</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463416">ачылуучу тизме</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13838_306445_462904"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A card, plug, or other device that connects pieces of hardware with the computer so that information can be moved from place to place. For example, standardized interfaces such as RS-232-C standard and SCSI enable communications between computers and printers or disks.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="306445">hardware interface</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="462904">интерфейс</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13838_68604_462904"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A card, plug, or other device that connects pieces of hardware with the computer so that information can be moved from place to place. For example, standardized interfaces such as RS-232-C standard and SCSI enable communications between computers and printers or disks.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="68604">interface</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="462904">интерфейс</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13842_253769_1495633"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A setting in which existing characters are replaced with newly typed characters.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="253769">overtype mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1495633">алмаштыруу режими</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13846_61010_462849"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A capability of many programs and operating systems to display advice or instructions for using their features when so requested by the user, as by a screen button or menu item or a function key.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="61010">help</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="462849">жардам</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13846_61011_462849"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A capability of many programs and operating systems to display advice or instructions for using their features when so requested by the user, as by a screen button or menu item or a function key.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="61011">online help</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="462849">жардам</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13863_107546_463170"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In facsimile and other optical technologies, to move a light-sensitive device across an image-bearing surface such as a page of text, converting the light and dark areas on the surface to binary digits that can be interpreted by a computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="107546">scan</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463170">скандоо</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13865_185672_1376472"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A small graphical symbol the user can insert into instant messages.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="185672">emoticon</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1376472">смайлик</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13873_122536_463277"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An individual song or other discrete piece of audio content.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="122536">track</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463277">жолчо</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13873_640881_463277"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An individual song or other discrete piece of audio content.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640881">audio track</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463277">жолчо</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13874_120089_1494215"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A button that represents an item or program that is open and running on your computer. For example, if you open Microsoft Word, and then minimize it, it will be displayed as a taskbar button, which you can then click when you want to maximize it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="120089">taskbar button</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1494215">иш панелинин баскычы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13883_43673_462699"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To detect, locate, and correct logical or syntactical errors in a program or malfunctions in hardware. In hardware contexts, the term troubleshoot is the term more often used, especially when the problem is a major one.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="43673">debug</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="462699">програмды түзөтүү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13888_237793_2097484"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A testing process that supplies structured but invalid input to software application programming interfaces (APIs) and network interfaces to maximize the likelihood of detecting errors that might lead to software vulnerabilities.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="237793">fuzz testing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2097484">так эмес сынак</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13888_767358_2097484"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A testing process that supplies structured but invalid input to software application programming interfaces (APIs) and network interfaces to maximize the likelihood of detecting errors that might lead to software vulnerabilities.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="767358">fuzzing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2097484">так эмес сынак</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13894_297011_1494216"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A program that installs other potentially unwanted software, such as adware or spyware. The license agreement of the bundling program may require these other components in order to function.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="297011">software bundler</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1494216">программалык камсыздоонун буу куралы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13902_142582_1890934"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A microphone feature that allows your input to be amplified so that it is made louder for use by the system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="142582">gain adjustment</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1890934">толукшуу жөндөөсү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13907_109815_1890876"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An executable program file that contains one or more compressed text or data files. When a user runs the program, it uncompresses the compressed files and stores them on the user's hard drive.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="109815">self-extracting file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1890876">өзүнөн өзү жандырылган файл</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13920_23913_462532"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Of or relating to communications systems in which the medium of transmission (such as a wire or fiber-optic cable) carries multiple messages at a time, each message modulated on its own carrier frequency by a modem.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="23913">broadband</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="462532">кең тилкелүү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adverb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13926_299909_1494217"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows technology that collects data when the system crashes or stops responding and sends it to Microsoft.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="299909">Windows Error Reporting</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1494217">Windows каталар отчёту</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13926_558472_1494217"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows technology that collects data when the system crashes or stops responding and sends it to Microsoft.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="558472">WER</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1494217">Windows каталар отчёту</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13932_186191_463619"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">One of the presets for 3D rotation effects. When selected, specifies that the object will be rotated isometrically.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="186191">isometric</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463619">изометрдик</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13946_109605_1494218"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To mark text, cells, and similar items that will be subject to a user action, such as copying text.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="109605">select</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1494218">тандоо</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13946_109605_1796853"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To mark text, cells, and similar items that will be subject to a user action, such as copying text.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="109605">select</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1796853">белгилөө</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13947_545693_2579322"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that provides a home for the Office Scrapbook, Compatibility Report, Project Palette and Reference Pane and is shown as a floating palette.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="545693">Toolbox</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2579322">Куралдар тактасы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13951_308301_464091"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The price at which a buyer has offered to purchase an item.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="308301">bid</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="464091">сунуш кылынган баа</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13955_1509436_1494219"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The menu item that allows the play back all of the items in a playlist once, in random order. Playback ends when all of the items in the list have been played one time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1509436">shuffle all</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1494219">аралаштыруу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13955_318745_1494219"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The menu item that allows the play back all of the items in a playlist once, in random order. Playback ends when all of the items in the list have been played one time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318745">shuffle</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1494219">аралаштыруу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1396_107623_463171"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An optical input device that uses light-sensing equipment to capture an image on paper or some other object. Captured image data is converted into binary files that can be stored and manipulated by computer programs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="107623">scanner</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463171">сканер</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13968_2587_1494220"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A network of computers, printers, and other devices located within a relatively limited area (for example, a building). A LAN enables any connected device to interact with any other on the network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2587">LAN</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1494220">жергиликтүү желе</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13968_2587_1494221"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A network of computers, printers, and other devices located within a relatively limited area (for example, a building). A LAN enables any connected device to interact with any other on the network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2587">LAN</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1494221">компаниялык желе</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="13968_2588_1494220"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A network of computers, printers, and other devices located within a relatively limited area (for example, a building). A LAN enables any connected device to interact with any other on the network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2588">local area network</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1494220">жергилик