ms</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2484165">Microsoft Голограммалар</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43437_2460385_2466090"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A network status tag that appears underneath an available Wi-Fi network and allows to select it in Windows network flyout.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2460385">Open, suggested</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2466090">Ачык, сунушталат</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43456_2461302_2464998"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The tab in the Exchange admin center where users can create and use In-Place eDiscovery searches and use In-Place Hold search results.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2461302">In-Place eDiscovery &amp; Hold</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2464998">Ордунда электрондук Табуу жана Кармоо</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43468_2721513_2723989"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that helps to isolate enterprise-defined untrusted sites based on a list of trusted web sites, cloud resources and internal networks defined by an enterprise administrator. Everything not on that list is considered untrusted.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2721513">Application Guard</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2723989">Колдонмо сакчысы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43468_2795831_2723989"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that helps to isolate enterprise-defined untrusted sites based on a list of trusted web sites, cloud resources and internal networks defined by an enterprise administrator. Everything not on that list is considered untrusted.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2795831">Microsoft Defender Application Guard</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2723989">Колдонмо сакчысы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43472_2795843_2466085"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The umbrella name for the Windows vulnerability mitigation features designed to address inherently technical attacks and prevent discovered vulnerabilities from being exploited.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2795843">Microsoft Defender Exploit Guard</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2466085">Windows коргоочусунун компьютердик кол салуудан сакчы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4349_58489_462835"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to an entire entity such as document, file, or program rather than to a restricted segment of it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="58489">global</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="462835">глобалдык</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43506_2462246_2466075"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The mixed-reality shell experience, in which content can be placed and used in virtual (or, in the case of HoloLens, real) surroundings.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2462246">mixed world</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2466075">аралашкан дүйнө</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4353_151854_2230383"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method of delivering digital media across a network in a continuous flow. The digital media is played by client software as it is received.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="151854">streaming</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2230383">медиа агымы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4353_2227182_2230383"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method of delivering digital media across a network in a continuous flow. The digital media is played by client software as it is received.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2227182">media streaming</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2230383">медиа агымы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43608_2464387_2466089"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A UI screen that appears in the Network flyout when a paid Wi-Fi hotspot is in range and paid Wi-Fi plans are available from Windows Store. A customer can then tap Connect with a data plan to open the Paid Wi-Fi &amp; Cellular app, choose a paid Wi-Fi data plan that’s offered from Windows Store, and then buy a plan using the payment information that’s stored in their Microsoft account.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2464387">Connect with a data plan</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2466089">Берилме планы менен туташуу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4362_153205_1493807"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A high-speed Internet connection. Broadband connections are typically 256 kilobytes per second (KBps) or faster.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="153205">broadband connection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1493807">кең тилкелүү туташуу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43627_2465102_2469757"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any very simple computer program that outputs or displays the words "Hello World" in some form to the user. Such a program is often created as an example, to introduce the basic syntax of a programming language to students or others new to that language.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2465102">Hello World</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2469757">Салам, дүйнө</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43628_2781062_2783438"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The offer for OneDrive for Business that includes Office Online and that is available through the User purchase subscription program.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2781062">OneDrive for Business with Office on the web (user purchased)</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2783438">OneDrive для бизнеса вебдеги Office менен (колдонуучу сатып алат)</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43662_2465860_2518403"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A web application on Xbox.com that allows Xbox One or PC gamers to design and purchase their own Xbox Wireless controller.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2465860">Xbox Design Lab</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2518403">Xbox Design Lab</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termN