ype="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44823_2524057_2576382"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A hardware accessory that allows you to take action in mixed reality. It tracks a precise position in space, allowing for fine-grained interaction with digital objects. When using a Windows Mixed Reality immersive headset, the motion controller is the primary way to take action.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524057">motion controller</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2576382">кыймыл аракет көзөмөлдөгүчү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44823_2524057_2576384"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A hardware accessory that allows you to take action in mixed reality. It tracks a precise position in space, allowing for fine-grained interaction with digital objects. When using a Windows Mixed Reality immersive headset, the motion controller is the primary way to take action.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524057">motion controller</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2576384">Windows Mixed Reality кыймыл аракет көзөмөлдөгүчү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44823_2531456_2576382"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A hardware accessory that allows you to take action in mixed reality. It tracks a precise position in space, allowing for fine-grained interaction with digital objects. When using a Windows Mixed Reality immersive headset, the motion controller is the primary way to take action.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2531456">Windows Mixed Reality motion controller</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2576382">кыймыл аракет көзөмөлдөгүчү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44823_2531456_2576384"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A hardware accessory that allows you to take action in mixed reality. It tracks a precise position in space, allowing for fine-grained interaction with digital objects. When using a Windows Mixed Reality immersive headset, the motion controller is the primary way to take action.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2531456">Windows Mixed Reality motion controller</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2576384">Windows Mixed Reality кыймыл аракет көзөмөлдөгүчү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44824_2524653_2529645"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows 10 update announced at Build 2017 and being released in the Sept-Nov 2017 timeframe.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524653">Windows 10 Fall Creators Update</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2529645">Windows 10 Fall Creators Update</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44825_2524668_2529638"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature in Windows Defender Security Center that monitors your device and provides you with information and recommendations in a Health report to address common issues with your storage capacity, device drivers, battery life, or Windows Update.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524668">Health Advisor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2529638">Кемчиликсиздикт кеңешчиси</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44826_2524671_2529637"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature in Windows Defender Security Center that helps you refresh your device by reinstalling and updating Windows — for example, if your device has performance issues or you have too many unnecessary apps.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig>