oor, building, wing, or office number. Place is associated with an emergency address to give a more exact location within a building.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2835571">place</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2840074">орун</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50139_2835572_2840079"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An emergency address that is assigned to each Calling Plan user; it is sometimes referred to as a static emergency address or address of record.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2835572">registered address</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2840079">катталган дарек</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5015_358327_1493847"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of taking a single-table database and breaking it into a set of smaller, related tables, with each table focused on a single topic or grouping of information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="358327">normalization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1493847">ченемдештирүү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50216_2841643_2845963"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A person who handles a call to a business such as to fill service requests, place orders, or connect to another respondent or another call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841643">call agent</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845963">агент</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50216_2841643_2845967"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A person who handles a call to a business such as to fill service requests, place orders, or connect to another respondent or another call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841643">call agent</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845967">чакыруулар агенти</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50216_2841644_2845963"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A person who handles a call to a business such as to fill service requests, place orders, or connect to another respondent or another call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841644">agent</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845963">агент</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50216_2841644_2845967"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A person who handles a call to a business such as to fill service requests, place orders, or connect to another respondent or another call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841644">agent</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845967">чакыруулар агенти</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50217_2841650_2845969"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a call queue, a method of sending calls to agents whereby routing of incoming calls is balanced so that each call agent gets the same number of calls from the queue.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841650">round robin</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845969">кезектештирүү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50219_2841716_2845968"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature of the Microsoft Teams Admin Center that shows detailed information about the devices, networks, and connectivity related to the calls and meetings for each user in a Microsoft Teams or Skype for Business tenant account. It is displayed on the user's Call History tab.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841716">Call Analytics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845968">Чакыруу талдоосу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50220_2841736_2845964"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Information that gives insight into usage patterns and activity.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841736">analytics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845964">Талдоо</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50221_2841755_2845965"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Microsoft teams, name of a tab on the Manage teams dialog that displays team analytics.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841755">Analytics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845965">талдоо</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50222_2841766_2845966"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a call queue, a method of sending calls to agents whereby the first call in the queue rings all call agents at the same time. The first call agent to pick up the call gets the call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841766">attendant routing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845966">жардамчыга каттатуу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50235_2842094_2845161"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">During an active meeting, to invite more people to join the meeting by dialing their phone number.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842094">dial out</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845161">терип чакыруу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50235_2842095_2845161"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">During an active meeting, to invite more people to join the meeting by dialing their phone number.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842095">dial-out</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845161">терип чакыруу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50236_2842096_2845160"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To join a conference call when the invited guest initiates the connection by phoning or by connecting through a computer with a conference ID or PIN. Contrast with dial out.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842096">dial in</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845160">терип кирүү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50238_2842098_2845164"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A function that automatically changes passwords after a certain time interval.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842098">password rotation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845164">пароль алмашуусу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50240_2842100_2845165"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A PowerPoint feature that allows the user to enter rehearsal mode and while speaking receive on-screen guidance about pacing, inclusive language, use of filler words, and culturally insensitive phrases. At the end of each rehearsal session, a detailed report with metrics for additional practice is provided.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842100">Presenter Coach</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845165">Коюп берүүчүнүн насаатчысы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50241_2842101_2845162"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An optional feature of Skype for Business Server that allows meeting attendees to join the audio portion of a meeting by calling in to the meeting from a phone.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842101">dial-in conferencing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845162">терүү аркылуу конференцияга чакыруу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50243_2842105_2845163"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Property of a private team that shows up in search results and is included in suggestions in the team gallery.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842105">discoverable</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845163">издеп табылуучу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5041_157347_2498569"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To terminate the current action before it is complete.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="157347">abandon</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2498569">токтотуу; баш тартуу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5060_129154_1493849"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In relational database management systems, a logical table created through the specification of one or more relational operations on one or more tables. A view is equivalent to a divided relation in the relational model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="129154">view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1493849">көрүнүшү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5069_160054_463536"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technique for converting a color in one color space to another color space. Typically, this conversion is from YUV colors from a video source to RGB for display.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="160054">color-space conversion</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463536">түс мейкиндигин алмаштыруу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5069_160054_463537"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technique for converting a color in one color space to another color space. Typically, this conversion is from YUV colors from a video source to RGB for display.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="160054">color-space conversion</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463537">түс мейкиндигин өзгөртүү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5069_210048_463536"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technique for converting a color in one color space to another color space. Typically, this conversion is from YUV colors from a video source to RGB for display.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="210048">color space conversion</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463536">түс мейкиндигин алмаштыруу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5069_210048_463537"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technique for converting a color in one color space to another color space. Typically, this conversion is from YUV colors from a video source to RGB for display.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="210048">color space conversion</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463537">түс мейкиндигин өзгөртүү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5070_346942_464389"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To provide or give.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="346942">deliver</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="464389">жеткирүү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5071_119170_1493850"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A character used to align lines and columns on screen and in print. Although a tab is visually indistinguishable from a series of blank spaces in most programs, the tab character and the space character are different to a computer. A tab is a single character and therefore can be added, deleted, or overtyped with a single keystroke.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="119170">tab character</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1493850">табуляция символу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5072_138277_2096439"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a shared file, information that is maintained about changes made in past editing sessions. The information includes the name of the person who made each change, when the change was made, and what data was changed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="138277">change history</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2096439">өзгөрүү тарыхы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5077_1546384_1493852"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A portion of a software window bounded by and separated from other portions by vertical or horizontal bars and having a separate function.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1546384">window pane</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1493852">панель</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5077_90456_1493852"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A portion of a software window bounded by and separated from other portions by vertical or horizontal bars and having a separate function.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="90456">pane</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1493852">панель</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5083_148996_1890981"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A shape in an organization chart that is placed below and connected to a superior (or manager) shape.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="148996">subordinate shape</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1890981">көз каранды калып</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5085_27452_1493853"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An (API) that is provided as part of Microsoft Windows. CryptoAPI provides a set of functions that allow applications to encrypt or digitally sign data in a flexible manner while providing protection for the user's sensitive private key data. Actual cryptographic operations are performed by independent modules known as (CSPs).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="27452">CAPI</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1493853">CAPI</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5085_27452_1495498"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An (API) that is provided as part of Microsoft Windows. CryptoAPI provides a set of functions that allow applications to encrypt or digitally sign data in a flexible manner while providing protection for the user's sensitive private key data. Actual cryptographic operations are performed by independent modules known as (CSPs).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="27452">CAPI</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1495498">Колдонмо программалоо интерфейсинин криптографиясы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5085_27453_1493853"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An (API) that is provided as part of Microsoft Windows. CryptoAPI provides a set of functions that allow applications to encrypt or digitally sign data in a flexible manner while providing protection for the user's sensitive private key data. Actual cryptographic operations are performed by independent modules known as (CSPs).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="27453">CryptoAPI</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1493853">CAPI</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5085_27453_1495498"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An (API) that is provided as part of Microsoft Windows. CryptoAPI provides a set of functions that allow applications to encrypt or digitally sign data in a flexible manner while providing protection for the user's sensitive private key data. Actual cryptographic operations are performed by independent modules known as (CSPs).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="27453">CryptoAPI</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1495498">Колдонмо программалоо интерфейсинин криптографиясы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5085_27454_1493853"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An (API) that is provided as part of Microsoft Windows. CryptoAPI provides a set of functions that allow applications to encrypt or digitally sign data in a flexible manner while providing protection for the user's sensitive private key data. Actual cryptographic operations are performed by independent modules known as (CSPs).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="27454">Cryptography Application Programming Interface</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1493853">CAPI</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5085_27454_1495498"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An (API) that is provided as part of Microsoft Windows. CryptoAPI provides a set of functions that allow applications to encrypt or digitally sign data in a flexible manner while providing protection for the user's sensitive private key data. Actual cryptographic operations are performed by independent modules known as (CSPs).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="27454">Cryptography Application Programming Interface</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1495498">Колдонмо программалоо интерфейсинин криптографиясы</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5090_115534_463215"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A special control added to a window, typically adjacent to the scroll bar, that allows a user to split a window or adjust a window split.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="115534">split box</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463215">бөлүүчү маркер</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5103_312764_464144"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Internet Explorer, a set of tabs you can store in your Favorites or as Home Page to reopen all tabs in the set in one go.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="312764">tab set</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="464144">кошумча барактар тобу</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5112_136266_463349"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Microsoft Windows multimedia file format for sound and videos that uses the Microsoft Resource Interchange File Format (RIFF) specification.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="136266">Audio Video Interleaved</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp