s, external disk drives, or other peripheral equipment.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="45147">device</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1493935">түзмөк</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6516_50772_462781"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of turning data into a stream of bits. Encoding is part of the serialization process that converts data into a stream of ones and zeros.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="50772">encoding</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="462781">коддоо</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6520_91124_1493936"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An effect created by simple, repeating designs such as vertical or horizontal lines.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="91124">pattern</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1493936">үлгү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6533_62030_1495528"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A postal address at which a person is normally resident.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="62030">home address</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1495528">үй дареги</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6538_360134_1499685"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A view that shows a graphical analysis of data in a datasheet or form. You can see different levels of detail or specify the layout by dragging fields and items or by showing and hiding items in the drop-down lists for the fields.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="360134">PivotChart view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1499685">PivotChart көрүнүшү</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6540_8001_1493937"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Interactive or animated content used on the Internet. Active content includes ActiveX controls and web browser add-ons.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="8001">active content</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1493937">активдүү маани</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6554_112160_1793319"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The paper that a publication is printed on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="112160">sheet</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1793319">барак</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6563_123499_463281"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A data structure containing zero or more nodes that are linked together in a hierarchy. If any nodes are present, one node is the root; each node except the root is the child of one and only one other node, and each node has zero or more nodes as children.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="123499">tree</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ky"><ntig><termGrp><term id="463281">дарак</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KGZ</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6573_5678_1493938"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A compressed file.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="5678">archive</term><termNote type="par